Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 57 CLINICAL DATA  56 y o  female with left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURED FROM SLIDES   GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION  MINOR FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NO DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS IDENTIFIED  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 19 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a h