Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 47 CLINICAL DATA  Status post left breast biopsy  intraductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INCLUDING ONE FOCUS AT INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  3  PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE CAVITY  LYMPH NODES  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IS PRESENT IN 1 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Infiltrating carcinoma is present within 0 5cm of the lateral inked resection margin  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Approximately half the residual carcinoma is infiltrative  Diagnosis by  David Weissmann  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 09 Staff Pathologist  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 3cm fragment of breast parenchyma with an overlying 6 5cm skin ellipse which has a 1 1cm centrally located unremarkable nipple  0 9cm from the nipple is a 3 5cm healing incision site  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm stellate shaped area of hemorrhagic tan soft parenchyma  coming to within 0 4cm of the nipple surface  0 4cm of the deep surgical resection margin  and 0 2cm from the lateral resection margin which is the closest margin  same side as incision site   Also received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary contents  is an 11 x 9 x 3cm mass of bloody adipose tissue  Sectioned to reveal several lymph nodes measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in greatest dimension  Section Code  A H  axillary lymph nodes  I  nipple  J K  nipple  tumor  and deep surgical resection margin  L  skin with incision site  tumor  deep and lateral resection margins  M  skin with incision site  tumor  and lateral resection margin  N  representative resection margin at 12 o clock   middle of incision site as designated 12 o clock   O  representative resection margin at 3 o clock  P  representative resection margin at 6 o clock  Q  representative resection margin at 9 o clock  R  section of tumor through firmest part  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Paul Snowden Russell  M D  John Abram Powelson  M D  PART A  BREAST TISSUE  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 58 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT IN THE WALL OF THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED INFERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY DISSECTION   ALL  12  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm overlying skin ellipse with a well healed 5 0cm long scar   The specimen has two stitches  the short stitch marking presumably the superior border and the long stitch marking the lateral end of the specimen   The specimen is inked black  the superior surface double inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from laterally to medially to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy cavity with indurated white borders up to 0 3cm in thickness  with fibrous strands extending to the deep and inferior margins  Section Code  A  lateral wall and biopsy cavity  B C D  representative sections of biopsy cavity   B and C are anterior and posterior extent of the specimen   E  lateral end of the biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of yellow fibroadipose tissue  containing multiple lymph nodes up to 2 0cm in diameter  Representative sections of each node are submitted in cassettes F through H  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLARY  RIGHT  , Unchecked.
