OVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right breast with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The specimen is surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE tan pink skin ellipse  There is an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm unremarkable tan areolar with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unremarkable nipple  No apparent scars or other gross abnormalities are noted  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect as per requisition  The anterior surface is inked blue  and the posterior is black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a diffusely gray white fibrous tissue with multiple enlarged  smooth walled cysts  Some of the cysts contain a gray tan grumous substance  The cyst walls are gray white and fibrous and average 0 1cm in thickness  The cysts come to 1 5cm of the posterior margin  and are diffusely distributed throughout the mammary tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm area of diffuse marked hemorrhage in the upper outer quadrant which comes to 4 0cm of the posterior margin  Within this hemorrhagic area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm lesion consistent with biopsy  which comes to 5 0cm of the deep margin  No other lesions or other gross abnormalities are noted  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals numerous tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 9cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as follows  A  Representative fibrous tissue to deep margin  B  Representative fibrous tissue including cysts to deep margin  C  Deep margin closest to hemorrhagic area  radial section   D F  Hemorrhagic area  with firm lesion  possibly representing previous biopsy site as D  G  Additional representative fibrous tissue including cysts  H  Multiple lymph nodes in toto  I J  Multiple lymph nodes in toto  K  One lymph node trisected  L O  Lymph node candidates  with one lymph node bisected as M  P Q  Representative upper outer quadrant  R S  Representative