 of the specimen  There are two white firm fibrous areas supromedially within 2 5cm of the previous biopsy site  cassette I   The larger of the two fibrous areas is focally cystic  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue  No lymph nodes are noted  Section code  A B  biopsy cavity in relation to closest margin  deep  C E  representative sections of remaining biopsy cavity with focal parenchymal changes F H  pink grey nodularity located inferiomedially in the parenchyma I  white focally cystic fibrous area supromedially to biopsy cavity  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
