lue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan white  firm  irregular  focally calcified mass with a central area of dark red hemorrhage corresponding to a prior needle tract  The mass abuts the superior  posterior and anterior margins and comes to 0 3cm of the inferior margin  The mass comes to 0 8cm of the lateral margin and focally abuts the medial margin  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE C  Radial sections of medial margin  D G  Mass to closest inked margins  H  Mass with surrounding tissue  I  Sections away from mass  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 2 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes  which are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE J  One 1 0cm lymph node  bisected  K  One 1 0cm lymph node  bisected  L  One 1 1cm lymph node  bisected  M  One 1 1cm lymph node  bisected  N  One 0 8cm lymph node  bisected  O  One 1 0cm lymph node  bisected  P  One 1 0cm lymph node  bisected  Q  One 0 4cm lymph node  bisected  R  Four whole lymph nodes  S  One 0 7cm lymph node  bisected  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  inferior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture on one surface designated by the surgeon as the new margin  The opposite surface is irregular  tan red and slightly firm  consistent with biopsy cavity  The sutured surface is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in T U  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with one sutured surface designated as the new margin  and an opposite surface which is tan and hemorrhagic consistent with biopsy cavity  The sutured surface is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as V W  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  lateral   are two portions of fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Each piece has a suture on one surface designated as the new margin which is inked black on each piece  The first piece is serially sectioned and submitted in X  The second piece is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in Y  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  superior   are two portions of fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Each has a suture on one surface designated as the new margin  which is inked black  and the first piece is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in Z  while the second piece is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in AA  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  deep   are multiple fragments of unoriented fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  entirely submitted in BB  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  anterior   is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue  which is unoriented and entirely submitted in CC DD  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D  O R  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  LERWILL  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Robin Scho