such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Rosemary Tambouret MD Signed On  06 MAY 04 at 16 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan  rubbery lymph node with minimal amount of attached fat  The entire specimen is frozen as FX  1 now in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan  rubbery lymph node with attached fat  The lymph node is bivalved and entirely frozen as FX  2 now in cassette B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  stitch at 12 o clock  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm left simple mastectomy specimen containing REMOVED_DATE x 11 2cm skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nipple  The skin contains 3 5cm linear scar lying 1 2cm from the superior skin resection margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm cavitary lesion corresponding to prior biopsy site  The biopsy site comes closest to within 1 2cm from the closest black inked posterior margin  Serial sectioning through the lateral aspect of the specimen reveals no axillary lymph nodes  The specimen is submitted as follows  Section Code  C F  Biopsy site to posterior margin  G H  Breast parenchyma away from the lesion  I  Scar   skin   J  Nipple  representative radial section  Resident  ANDRAS SCHAFFER  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   EXCISION  CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  AWAIT SENTINEL NODE WORKUP  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  L