imen which localizes the calcifications  The specimen is serially sectioned from the medial to the lateral aspect to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm soft  tan  nodular lesion in the vicinity of the microcalcification  The lesion extends to 0 4cm of the posterior margin  0 9cm to the anterior margin  1 3cm to the inferior margin  0 8cm to the superior margin  1 5cm to the medial margin and greater than 2 0cm to the lateral margin  The remainder of the tissue consist predominantly of adipose tissue with a small amount of it to be soft  white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The area of microcalcification is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The nodular lesion is in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Paula Arnell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results  An E cadherin immunoperoxidase stain is non contributory as the focus of interest is not present on the deeper sections  Addendum  2 by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE