Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 MAY 97 ACCESSIONED ON  12 MAY 97 at 10 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  PRESENT AS THREE DISCONTINUOUS FOCI IN TWO OF EIGHT SLIDES INVOLVING THE INFERIOR ASPECT OF THE SPECIMEN  BOTH EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INFERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  NOTE  NO RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  ALL RESECTION MARGINS APPEAR FREE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  BLOOD VASCULAR AND LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION IS NOT SEEN  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  14 MAY 97 at 19 41                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labelled with the patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm piece of breast tissue attached to a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of skin ellipse  with a long stitch for designating the lateral margin and a short stitch for the superior margin  The skin ellipse contains a 3 0cm surgical scar  The specimen is inked black superiorly and blue inferiorly  and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm biopsy cavity  0 3cm from the superior resection margin  0 3cm from the posterior resection margin  0 4cm from the inferior resection margin  0 4cm from the lateral resection margin  and 2 0cm from the skin surface  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by fat necrosis  which extends to the superior  posterior  lateral  and medial resection margins at multiple points  Sectioning of the adjacent tissue reveals a tan yellow fibrofatty cut surface in addition to the fat necrosis  and no nodular lesion is identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A H  All sections include superior and inferior margins  Section Code  AandB   biopsy cavity with posterior margin  CandD   biopsy cavity with lateral margin  EandF   biopsy cavity with medial margin  G   biopsy cavity with anterior margin and skin  H   adjacent tissue with lateral margin  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  24 MAY 96 at 12 41 CLINICAL DATA  73 year old woman with a left breast mass found on screening mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE I III   FOCALLY PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite blood vessel or lymphatic vesselinvasion is identified  The frozen section gross impression is confirmed  2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM PATTERNS  LOW GRADE   ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND FOCALLY LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  3 FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 MAY 96 at 12 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of breast with a localizing wire in place and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 9cm  white  stellate firm nodule located adjacent to an inked resection margin  All fibrous tissue is submitted in A through J  with the suspicious nodule in A through D  remaining non  suspicious fatty tissue   1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm   is not submitted  No other masses are seen    Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Diane Elise Rich  M D  PART   BREAST TISSUE  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
