rs by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 59     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  RESULTS PENDING The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 16 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is submitted in two parts each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Received fresh in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  On the specimen is an ellipse of skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm with a nipple and areola measuring 2 0cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity immediately adjacent to the ellipse of skin  The cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and a stitch is present to indicate the previous biopsy site  This ar