e F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen which consists of a left breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with an inverted T shaped overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm axillary tail  The skin surface is studded with multiple REMOVED_DATE to 0 6cm skin colored papules diffusely across its surface  The nipple is unremarkable and no definitive old scars are identified  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm tan white stellate infiltrating nodule is identified corresponding to the 2 o clock region of the specimen  It comes to 0 5cm from the closest  anterior  margin and 1 2cm from the posterior margin  As well  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm tan white stellate infiltrating nodule is present corresponding to the 10 o clock region of the specimen and it is 1 5cm from the closest  posterior  margin  Multiple smaller  similar in appearance nodules are present throughout the breast parenchyma ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm in greatest dimension  The closest of which approaches the posterior margin to 0 8cm  They are present primarily in the mid portion of the specimen  Axillary lymph nodes as large as 1 6cm in greatest dimension are identified  The cut surface is firm and tan pink  Section code  G   2 o clock mass and sections of posterior margin adjacent to mass  H   2 o clock mass and adjacent anterior margin I  representative section of 10 o clock lesion and representative section of 10 o clock region with adjacent closest posterior margin  J   representative section of 10 o clock lesion with adjacent anterior margin K M  representative sections of other parenchymal nodules and representative section of skin papule  N R  axillary lymph nodes completely submitted S   axillary lymph node bivalved  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  are multiple fragments of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with attached skin aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  Serial sections reveal predominantly unremarkable breast parenchyma with few focal ill defined tan white fibrous areas  The skin surface has multiple REMOVED_DATE to 0 6cm skin colored papules  Section code  T  representative section of skin U Y  ten representative sections of breast parenchyma  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  May Wakamatsu  M D  Rosa Sung Eun Choi  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  ADNEXA  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  ADNEXA  RIGHT   EXCISION PART C  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL PART D  LYMPH NODES   ADDITIONAL AXILLARY    EXCISION PART E  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART F  BREAST  LEFT   MAMMOPLASTY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 40 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    WITH TUBULAR FEATURES  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION SLIDE   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  ADJACENT TO  BUT NOT DISTANT FROM  INFILTRATING TUMOR  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROSIS  CYSTS AND FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  4  MONCKEBERG S MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS OF ARTERIES  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a breast biopsy containing a 1 1cm in greatest diameter stellate  firm  tan mass approaching an inked margin  Representative tissue is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in A  remainder of mass in B through D with representative surrounding in E through G  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND CRIBRIFORM DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
