 defined fibrotic healing biopsy site  which is present approximately between the 6 and 7 o clock positions  and which abuts the posterior inked margin and lies beneath the well healed linear skin scar  The metallic clip is grossly appreciated  The remaining breast parenchyma contains tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with scant amount of tan white fibrous tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly appreciated in the upper outer quadrant tissue  where the axillary tail stitch is located  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the biopsy site  including the closest posterior and anterior inked margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma at the level of the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma at the level of the inner lower quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast skin margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of fragmented tan white skin  which is inked black and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the t