Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 MAY 99 ACCESSIONED ON  07 MAY 99 at 15 40 CLINICAL DATA  None given                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     COLON  FOCAL ILEAL ISCHEMIA WITH TRANSMURAL NECROSIS  PERFORATION  AND EXTRAMURAL ABSCESS FORMATION ASSOCIATED WITH MESENTERIC ARTERIAL THROMBOSIS AND COMPLETE OCCLUSION  SLIDE D   MARGINS OF RESECTION ARE HISTOLOGICALLY VIABLE  BREAST  LEFT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Residual invasive carcinoma is not seen  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins are free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 99 at 10 49 Consulting Pathologist s   Carolyn C  Compton  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  L Breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 10 8cm ellipse of tan nipple bearing skin  On the skin  there is a 3 8cm curvilinear  healing scar that runs along the superior aspect of the nipple  which is inverted  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm healing biopsy cavity with a tan pink lining membrane  The cavity comes to 1 8cm from the posterior margin and 1 8cm from the anteroinferior margin  and grossly abuts the skin  The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity are submitted from medial to lateral in Cassettes H K  with the inverted nipple in Cassette I  The closest posterior margin is submitted in Cassette L  the closest anteroinferior margin is submitted in Cassette M  and representative sections of unremarkable parenchyma are also in Cassettes L M  as well as N O  No lymph nodes are found in the axillary portion of the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Ileal Colon   is an 8 0cm portion of cecum and a 45 0cm portion of attached ileum  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm transmural defect  located at 7 0cm from the ileocecal junction and the surrounding mesentery necrosis and fibrinous adhesions  Opening the specimen reveals that the perforation site has a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm area showing mucosal necrosis with yellow brown discoloration and sharp demarcation from adjacent dark red mucosa  The entire ileal colon specimen is examined to find no definite tumor lesion on the mucosal surface  Sectioning of the mesentery revealed nodular  appearing adhesions and fat necrosis  Also received in the same container is a 10 0cm unoriented portion of small intestine with a side to side anastomosis to a 7 0cm portion of the small intestine  The anastomosis site has a fresh suture  and the mucosa of both small intestine fragments are dark red with edema  SECTION CODE  A   Proximal ileal resection margin  B   Distal colonic resection margin  C   Representative section from the perforation site  D   Representative section from the mesentery  E   Anastomosis site  F G  End from the anastomosis  Gross Description by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  COLON PART B  BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
