dipose tissue  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked blue  the posterior black  Serial sectioning of the specimen reveals a grossly well circumscribed  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm cavity  The lining of the cavity is tan red  glistening and smooth  and the parenchyma surrounding the cavity is focally indurated up to a thickness of 1 5cm away from the cavity lining  The cavity comes focally to within 0 2cm of the posterior margin  The cavity comes to within 3 5cm of the superior  6 5cm of the inferior  3 5cm of the lateral  and 5 0cm of the medial margins  The cavity also comes to within 2 5cm of the anterior resection margin and it is a distance of 2 8cm from the previously described periareolar scar  The tissue between the cavity and the anterior skin ellipse is focally indurated  however no discrete masses are identified  The remainder of the parenchyma is tan yellow and does not show gross abnormalities  with the exception of a tan white  indurated fibrous area of tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm that is located 2 5cm medially from the medial edge of the previously described cavity  This fibrous area comes to within 2 5cm of the posterior margin  4 5cm of the anterior margin  5 5cm of the inferior margin  6 0cm of the superior margin  3 0cm of the medial margin and 18 0cm from the lateral margin  Lymph nodes are not identified in the specimen  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity with respect to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity with respect to closest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of cavity with respect to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section away from the cavity and in the area of previously described 4 0cm fibrous indurated area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm tissue  located anterior and lateral to the biopsy cavity  with respect to the anterior margin Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lateral tissue   are multiple fragments of tan yellow adipose tissue measuring in aggregate of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  These fragment are not oriented  The tissue is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable adipose tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections of the tissue are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary nodes   are two pieces of soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The first piece represents a likely lymph node  which is bivalved and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional candidate lymph nodes are identified and submitted intact in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Michael H Roehrl M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael H Roehrl M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL LATERAL   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT ADDITIONAL AXILLA   DISSECTION  report_end  , Unchecked.
