Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 22 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with a left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  85    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  15    CRIBRIFORM AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive tumor measures 1 4cm in greatest diameter  and approaches to within 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  A focus of carcinoma in situ is present at the cauterized margin  There is no definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 19 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST LEFT  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with needle localization and accompanied by roentgenogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  firm  white  ill defined  non gritty nodule which comes to within 0 2cm of the closest inked margin  The nodule corresponds to the radiographic lesion over the thick portion of the wire  The mass has a central red hemorrhagic coloration  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  corresponding to the course of the wire  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in A through J  with the rest of the nodule in C through F  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST MASS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
