Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 57 CLINICAL DATA  70 year old female with right breast biopsy in REMOVED_DATE showing infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST   LUMPECTOMY   1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90 95    REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III    SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  All margins appear free of invasive carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ  SOFT TISSUE   AXILLARY CONTENTS    ALL  THIRTEEN  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm lumpectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm skin ellipse  Centrally  the skin contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm area of induration  with accentuated dermal markings  No scars are noted  Directly underlying the skin changes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  stellate and lobular  tan yellow mass  extending to within 2 0cm of the deep resection margin  and 1 5cm of the closest lateral resection surface  The parenchyma fibrous septae extends from the mass and abut the inked surfaces  the remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable  Section Code  A B  skin with underlying mass  C  lateral margin  D  deep margin  E  mass  F G H  septae extending to inked surfaces  Labeled  Axillary contents  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of fatty tissue  dissected to reveal approximately 13 lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum diameter  soft to rubbery  All nodes submitted in I J K  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B  RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
